annotator_A_json:
{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "text": "Sperm banks could one day be set up in space, scientists have predicted.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "Frozen samples that were exposed to microgravity conditions and those kept in normal conditions appear to keep similar characteristics",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "The results of the research suggest frozen sperm could be sent into space and \"open the possibility of creating a human sperm bank outside of Earth\".",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "But more research is needed to fully understand the effect of space conditions, scientists have said.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "The study was presented at the European Society of Human Reproduction and Embryology annual meeting in Vienna, Austria.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "The scientists conducting the study said little is known about the effect of different gravity levels on sperm.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Dr Montserrat Boada, from Dexeus Women's Health in Barcelona, said: \"Some studies suggest a significant decrease in the motility of human fresh sperm sample.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "\"But nothing has been reported on the possible effects of gravitational differences on frozen human gametes, in which state they could be transported from Earth to space.\"",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "The researchers used sperm from 10 healthy donors, exposing some of the samples to microgravity using a small aerobatic aircraft.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "The samples were then analyzed for concentration, motility and DNA fragmentation - tests which are all performed to check for fertility.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "No significant differences were found between the samples kept on the ground and those exposed to microgravity, according to the study.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "\"The lack of differences observed in the sperm characteristics between frozen samples exposed to microgravity and those maintained in ground conditions open the possibility of safely transporting male gametes to space and considering the possibility of creating a human sperm bank outside of Earth,\" the researchers said.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "However they added that this is a preliminary study, and they need to validate their findings with more samples and expose the sperm to space-like conditions for longer periods of time.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "\"Our best option will be to perform the experiment using real spaceflight but access is very limited,\" Dr Boada said.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 13
    }
  ]
}

